class:: LevyFlight
summary:: Unbounded stochastic transport with independent symmetric stable increments
categories:: UGens>Generators>Stochastic>Processes
related:: Classes/TStableRand, Classes/TLevyRand, Classes/OUProcess, Classes/FBrownianMotion, Classes/JumpDiffusion, Guides/Stochastica

description::
Accumulates symmetric alpha-stable increments into a position. Lower alpha permits rare large relocations among smaller movements. This memory is accumulated position, not correlated increments: successive innovations are independent. FBrownianMotion models increment correlation through a finite-memory approximation; OUProcess pulls toward a center; LevyFlight does neither. TStableRand samples individual stable values, while TLevyRand is a one-sided Levy distribution, not this symmetric motion.

Each calculation advances code::x += drift*dt + scale*dt.pow(1/alpha)*S::, with S a unit symmetric stable variable in the existing Nolan S0 convention. For beta=0 its characteristic function is code::exp(-abs(t).pow(alpha))::. Alpha=2 is Gaussian with increment variance code::2*scale*scale*dt::; alpha=1 is Cauchy. For alpha below two the stable variance is infinite, and for alpha at most one the mean is undefined. A symmetric finite sample is not evidence of a finite population mean.

The server reuses the bounded Chambers–Mallows–Stuck sampler used by TStableRand. Source: Nolan's link::https://edspace.american.edu/jpnolan/wp-content/uploads/sites/1720/2020/09/Chap1.pdf:: stable-distribution reference. The elapsed interval includes timeScale and is one sample for .ar or one block for .kr. Equal model time has the same stable law with fixed parameters, though sequences differ between rates.

State and finite increments remain unbounded doubles internally. They are not wrapped, folded or normalized. Only float serialization saturates at machine range. Non-finite updates restore initial and emit a zero increment, keeping the runtime RNG position; an explicit reset additionally rewinds it. Extremely small alpha or large scales can exceed numeric range, so recovery truncates those otherwise unrepresentable paths. Each calculation has bounded constant work and no allocation. Discontinuities and fast sonification can alias.

Like vanilla link::Classes/BrownNoise::, this remembers a random walk position. BrownNoise is a bounded audio-noise generator; LevyFlight exposes unbounded transport and stable rather than bounded uniform increments.

