subsection:: See also
link::Classes/TStableRand::, link::Classes/TLevyRand::, link::Classes/OUProcess::, link::Classes/FBrownianMotion::, link::Classes/JumpDiffusion::, link::Guides/Stochastica::

classmethods::
method:: ar, kr
argument:: alpha
Stable exponent, clipped to 0.01..2, sampled each calculation. Smaller values yield heavier tails; non-finite values use the lower bound.
argument:: scale
Stable scale per unit model time, interpreted by magnitude; non-finite becomes zero. Alpha=2 corresponds to Brownian diffusion amplitude sqrt(2)*scale.
argument:: drift
Finite deterministic displacement per model second. Non-finite becomes zero.
argument:: timeScale
Nonnegative model seconds per real second. Nonpositive/non-finite values hold state and emit zero increment.
argument:: initial
Position at construction, reset or numerical recovery. Non-finite becomes zero.
argument:: seed
Local PCG32 seed; nonzero repeats a sequence. Zero derives from the Synth RNG only at construction.
argument:: reset
Nonpositive-to-positive edge restores initial and the original local seed, emits zero increment and skips evolution. Held positive does not repeat.
returns::
Two outputs: code::[state, increment]::. The second is the complete displacement on this calculation, including drift. Construction emits initial and zero increment.

examples::
subsection:: Minimal register motion
code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar((60 + LevyFlight.kr(1.2, 3, seed: 57)[0]).clip(30, 96).midicps, 0, 0.07) ! 2 }.play
)
::

subsection:: Relocations and an unchanged voice
The left channel has Gaussian transport, the right heavy-tailed transport. Clipping is an explicit pitch-domain decision; the raw paths in the figure are not clipped. Neither process returns to a center, so a long run may remain at a pitch boundary.
code::
(
{
    [2, 1.2].collect { |alpha|
        var position = LevyFlight.kr(alpha, 4, seed: 57)[0];
        var pitch = (60 + position).clip(30, 96);
        SinOsc.ar(pitch.midicps, 0, 0.065)
    } * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.05)
}.play
)
::
